import mundane theorem    stdlib/sums/sum-extended
import mundane theorem    stdlib/sums/sum-single

theorem sum-of-eight-i-minus-five
  note        By induction on n: adding 8(k + 1) − 5 to 4k² − k gives
              4(k + 1)² − (k + 1).
  let n ∈ ℕ                                                           (H1)
  then Σ(i = 1 to n) (8i − 5) = 4n² − n

let S(m) = Σ(j = 1 to m) (8j − 5), for m ∈ ℕ                          (D1)
       reads the sum of the first m terms 8j − 5

1.  For all k ∈ ℕ, S(k) = 4k² − k.
    induction on k starting at 1

    base
    1.1.  S(1) = 4·1² − 1
          calculation
            S(1) = Σ(j = 1 to 1) (8j − 5)   D1
                 = 8·1 − 5                  mun:sum-single a := 1
                 = 4·1² − 1                 arithmetic

    step
    let k ∈ ℕ                                                         (K)
    assume step 1 is true for k, the induction hypothesis             (IH)

    1.2.  S(k + 1) = S(k) + (8(k + 1) − 5)
          calculation
            S(k + 1) = Σ(j = 1 to k + 1) (8j − 5)                        D1
                     = Σ(j = 1 to k) (8j − 5) + (8(k + 1) − 5)           mun:sum-extended a := 1, n := k
                     = S(k) + (8(k + 1) − 5)                             D1
          requires k ≥ 1: from K

    1.3.  S(k + 1) = 4(k + 1)² − (k + 1)
          calculation
            S(k + 1) = S(k) + (8(k + 1) − 5)            1.2
                     = 4k² − k + (8(k + 1) − 5)         substitute IH
                     = 4(k + 1)² − (k + 1)              algebra

2.  Σ(i = 1 to n) (8i − 5) = 4n² − n
    calculation
      Σ(i = 1 to n) (8i − 5) = S(n)          D1
                             = 4n² − n       instantiate k := n in line 1
